    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚙️ One-time Setup\n\n**1. Google Sheets — API Keys tab**\nIn your existing sheet, create a new tab named **`API Keys`** with these exact column headers in row 1:\n`api_key` | `owner` | `daily_limit` | `daily_count` | `last_reset` | `active`\n\nAdd one row per user:\n- `api_key`: a long random string (generate with `openssl rand -hex 16`)\n- `owner`: their name\n- `daily_limit`: `5`\n- `daily_count`: `0`\n- `last_reset`: `2000-01-01`\n- `active`: `yes`\n\nTo revoke a key: set `active` → `no`. To reset manually: set `daily_count` → `0`.\n\n**2. Credentials needed**\n- **Google Sheets**: already set up ✓\n- **Google Gemini**: bind on `Gemini Chat Model` sub-node\n- **Serper.dev Header Auth**: bind on `Search Google Maps via Serper`\n- **SMTP**: create in n8n → Credentials → New → SMTP. Bind on both email send nodes. Also set `fromEmail` in both nodes.\n\n**3. Webhook URL**\nOnce workflow is **Active**, your webhook URL is:\n`https://YOUR_N8N_DOMAIN/webhook/lead-generation`\nUpdate `WEBHOOK_URL` in `lead-form.html` to match.\n\n**4. CORS (if form is on a different domain)**\nSet `N8N_CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN=*` (or your domain) in n8n's environment.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "8d7d866d-a11f-4f06-9c6e-d2c3d935a1e3",
